        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "EST II works in radians: a full turn is \\(2\\pi\\approx6.28\\), not \\(360°\\). \\(P=(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)\\) as above.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Graphs of trigonometric functions</h3>The function \\( y=A\\sin(Bx+C)+D \\) has amplitude \\( |A| \\), period \\( \\dfrac{2\\pi}{B} \\), phase shift \\( -C/B \\), and vertical shift \\( D \\). Knowing how to read these parameters from a graph or equation is a core EST II skill.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Advanced Trigonometry",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Unit circle: \\((\\cos\\theta, \\sin\\theta)\\). Key identities: \\(\\tan\\theta = \\sin\\theta/\\cos\\theta\\); \\(\\sec\\theta = 1/\\cos\\theta\\). Double angle: \\(\\sin 2\\theta = 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\); \\(\\cos 2\\theta = 1-2\\sin^2\\theta\\). <strong>Law of cosines:</strong> \\(c^2 = a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C\\). <strong>Area:</strong> \\(\\tfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Non-right triangle (Law of Sines)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "In triangle \\(ABC\\): \\(a=8\\), \\(B=35°\\), \\(C=75°\\). Find side \\(b\\). <p>\\(A = 180°-35°-75° = 70°\\). By sine rule: \\(\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B} = \\dfrac{a}{\\sin A} \\Rightarrow b = \\dfrac{8\\sin 35°}{\\sin 70°} \\approx \\dfrac{4.589}{0.9397} \\approx 4.88\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find all solutions of \\(\\cos 2\\theta = \\cos\\theta\\) for \\(0° \\leq \\theta \\leq 360°\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(2\\cos^2\\theta-1 = \\cos\\theta \\Rightarrow 2\\cos^2\\theta-\\cos\\theta-1=0 \\Rightarrow (2\\cos\\theta+1)(\\cos\\theta-1)=0\\). \\(\\cos\\theta=1 \\Rightarrow \\theta=0°\\); \\(\\cos\\theta=-1/2 \\Rightarrow \\theta=120°, 240°\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
